Usages:
  conventions: .goga/usages/conventions.md

Annotations: |
  Use `conventions` for code writing rules and testing.
  The cell packages domain skills as data files inside the wheel and exposes them through
  a cached facade — one filesystem read per skill per runtime, never per request.
  Each skill lives in its own subdirectory as SKILL.md; the content belongs to the skill
  file alone and is never restated in any manifest.

---
"load_skill(name: str) -> text: str":
  location: __init__.py
  annotations: |
    Read a packaged skill by name — the content is cached after the first read.

    `name`: the skill directory name under the cell package (e.g. playwright).
    `text`: the verbatim content of the skill's SKILL.md.

    Algorithm:
    1. The process-level cache holds the content — a hit returns without touching the filesystem
    2. A miss reads SKILL.md from the named subdirectory through importlib.resources
    3. The content lands in the cache and returns

    Requirements:
    - One filesystem read per skill per runtime — the cache is process-level and unconditional
    - The SKILL.md files ship in the wheel via package-data
    - No validation of the content — the consumer owns the interpretation

